Of course it won't stop anybody from running nethack ...
all they need is a copy of the shell, which sets up the variables
and then calls the SAME executable!  We ignore that problems here,
and our system runs the System V cron code that does a chmod -x
/usr/games/* during work hours and chmod +x at lunch and 5:00.
(Well, it's actually modified a bit, because /usr/games/fortune HAS
to work at all times or some people can't log in ...)
This doesn't really do the job either, but people mostly behave.

